# Backend Architecture Guidelines (Java)

Purpose: backend single source of truth for architecture, implementation order, testing, and backend handover format.

## Stack Profile

- Language: Java 17+
- Build: Maven or Gradle

## Project Structure Expectations

- Keep entry points thin and delegate to services.
- Keep business logic in service classes.
- Keep persistence logic in repository classes.
- Keep DTOs, entities, and mappers separated by responsibility.
- Use DTOs at API boundaries; do not replace persistence entities with DTOs in the repository layer.
- Follow project conventions for package and class naming.

## Code Quality

- Use PMD, SpotBugs, and ArchUnit to analyze code after it is implemented.
- Prefer service-layer tests as the default verification layer.

